1
00:00:00,937 --> 00:00:04,317
(Leonard:)Sheldon, we agreed we'd do something
different tonight.

2
00:00:04,483 --> 00:00:07,073
(Sheldon:)All right. Let's go
to the comic book store.

3
00:00:07,235 --> 00:00:09,195
(Raj:)We went to the comic book store
last night.

4
00:00:09,362 --> 00:00:11,952
(Sheldon:)Last night was Wednesday.
Wednesday is comic-book night.

5
00:00:12,115 --> 00:00:17,535
(Sheldon:)We'll be going on Thursday because
it's Anything Can Happen Thursday.

6
00:00:18,038 --> 00:00:22,208
(Leonard:)Way to think outside but pressed right up
against the box, Sheldon.

7
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:23,835
What are we gonna do tonight?

8
00:00:24,002 --> 00:00:26,172
(Howard:)If I may proffer a suggestion...

9
00:00:26,338 --> 00:00:31,338
(Howard:)...in bars all across this great nation
of ours, Thursday night is Ladies' Night.

10
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:34,430
(Howard:)As the evening progresses,
we will get better-looking...

11
00:00:34,596 --> 00:00:37,516
...courtesy of 99-cent margaritas
and two-for-one Jell-O shots.

12
00:00:40,852 --> 00:00:44,942
(Leonard:)Come on, Howard, the odds of us picking
up girls in a bar are practically zero.

13
00:00:45,107 --> 00:00:47,397
Oh. Really?
Are you familiar with the Drake equation?

14
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:50,237
(Sheldon:)The one that estimates the odds
of contact with extraterrestrials...

15
00:00:50,403 --> 00:00:53,153
(Sheldon:)...by calculating the product
of series of fractional values...

16
00:00:53,323 --> 00:00:55,743
...such as stars
with planets likely to develop life?

17
00:00:55,909 --> 00:01:04,019
(Sheldon:)N equals R times FP times NE times FL
times Fl times FC times L?

